{"data": [{"author_id": "68746721", "created_at": "2026-10-24T13:01:13.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113979122103759273"], "id": "2113979122103759273", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 213, "impression_count": 81392, "like_count": 755, "quote_count": 15, "reply_count": 89, "retweet_count": 32}, "text": "Symbolic learning works", "url": "https://x.com/fchollet/status/2113979122103759273"}, {"author_id": "25098482", "created_at": "2026-10-24T12:30:02.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113971276104740886"], "id": "2113971276104740886", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 43, "impression_count": 59481, "like_count": 374, "quote_count": 13, "reply_count": 25, "retweet_count": 113}, "text": "In emerging market and developing economies, growth is projected to slow to 3.7% in 2026 before recovering to 4.4% in 2027, with prospects shaped by commodity dependence, sensitivity to financial conditions, policy frameworks, and position in the global technology value chain. https://t.co/mMzgpDWo8c", "url": "https://x.com/IMFNews/status/2113971276104740886"}, {"author_id": "25098482", "created_at": "2026-10-24T08:30:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113910873320575448"], "id": "2113910873320575448", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 17, "impression_count": 25064, "like_count": 170, "quote_count": 5, "reply_count": 11, "retweet_count": 42}, "text": "The global economy proved resilient through pandemic, war, inflation, and trade tension, but strains are showing. Policymakers must move from coping to rebuilding, and countries should build resilience together. Read @STenreyro’s blog for more. https://t.co/javlPkw7Ks https://t.co/uTpCKLHZwN", "url": "https://x.com/IMFNews/status/2113910873320575448"}, {"author_id": "83466368", "created_at": "2026-10-24T06:00:56.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113873354578960423"], "id": "2113873354578960423", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 51, "impression_count": 42057, "like_count": 173, "quote_count": 39, "reply_count": 274, "retweet_count": 53}, "text": "The digital euro will bring the benefits of cash into the digital age: a secure form of public money that protects privacy and is accepted across the euro area, says ECB Executive Board member Piero Cipollone to @MilanoFinanza.\n\nRead the interview https://t.co/FC9TvVPpOP https://t.co/7FRB01HBwA", "url": "https://x.com/ecb/status/2113873354578960423"}, {"author_id": "1214528593", "created_at": "2026-10-24T02:03:43.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113813659369853033"], "id": "2113813659369853033", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 2486, "like_count": 15, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2113812792209752432", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Dudes rock https://t.co/eGOeMayygN", "url": "https://x.com/Miles_Brundage/status/2113813659369853033"}, {"author_id": "279036722", "created_at": "2026-10-23T22:06:19.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113753913593827624"], "id": "2113753913593827624", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 43, "impression_count": 14631, "like_count": 95, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 7, "retweet_count": 6}, "text": "If you subscribe to Econvitals Daily Economic Update you would just have gotten this in your inbox.\n\nI find it reliable, readable and reasonably compressive—but not especially edgy, original or idiosyncratic.\n\nhttps://t.co/NM6bWOhhRJ https://t.co/cBxWsvyiXj", "url": "https://x.com/jasonfurman/status/2113753913593827624"}, {"author_id": "1214528593", "created_at": "2026-10-23T22:05:43.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113753761768411424"], "id": "2113753761768411424", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 29, "impression_count": 26786, "like_count": 360, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 21, "retweet_count": 9}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2113729700707053710", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Well Wall Street is dumb https://t.co/24GTTMMDBm", "url": "https://x.com/Miles_Brundage/status/2113753761768411424"}, {"author_id": "1214528593", "created_at": "2026-10-23T21:35:21.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113746119301963885"], "id": "2113746119301963885", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 14, "impression_count": 7305, "like_count": 87, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 9, "retweet_count": 3}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2113717691420950973", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Don’t have time to make the meme but something something @polynoamial apology form https://t.co/RZVPTWV9lx", "url": "https://x.com/Miles_Brundage/status/2113746119301963885"}, {"author_id": "25098482", "created_at": "2026-10-23T21:30:12.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113744825623445740"], "id": "2113744825623445740", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 89, "impression_count": 46977, "like_count": 203, "quote_count": 5, "reply_count": 11, "retweet_count": 51}, "text": "How did advanced economies cut their debt roughly in half after WWII? In this Analytical Corner, Neil Shenai explains that the biggest driver wasn't growth or fiscal consolidation. It was financial repression. https://t.co/BvlYbPGiUZ https://t.co/t0SY8GKSNz", "url": "https://x.com/IMFNews/status/2113744825623445740"}, {"author_id": "279036722", "created_at": "2026-10-23T21:24:12.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113743316105752832"], "id": "2113743316105752832", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 15, "impression_count": 14119, "like_count": 73, "quote_count": 3, "reply_count": 5, "retweet_count": 8}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2113738508959358989", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Looks like we'll see very strong growth for Q3 GDP, data out on Thursday.\n\nEconvitals Composite tracking is for GDP growth of 3.2% in Q3.\n\nThe composite tracker is a weighted average of several other measures--including Econvitals own estimate (2.4%).\n\nPrivate demand *much* https://t.co/089tqvebN9", "url": "https://x.com/jasonfurman/status/2113743316105752832"}], "includes": {"users": [{"id": "68746721", "name": "François Chollet", "username": "fchollet"},